# =============================================================================
# Worker env bundle for muaddib self-hosting.
# Copy to `.muaddib/secrets.env` (gitignored) — spawn-worker.sh reads it directly.
#
# Project-scoped secrets only — a credential limited to this repo, not your
# account. CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is NOT here: it's account-level (tied to
# the Claude subscription, not any one repo) and lives in
# ~/.muaddib/conductor-secrets.env instead — see that file's own .example.
#
# This is genuinely near-empty right now, not under-filled-in:
#  - muaddib itself has no config.ts-style required env vars, no DB, and no
#    third-party service integrations of its own to configure here.
#  - LINEAR_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed — muaddib's own tickets live in
#    GitHub Issues (rphovley/muaddib), never Linear. Do not add a Linear key
#    here to work around a GitHub-ticket-source gap; file/fix that gap instead
#    (see e.g. #70's fetch-ticket.js routing fix).
# =============================================================================

# GitHub fine-grained PAT, scoped to only this repository (not all repos).
# Everywhere GITHUB_TOKEN is actually used in this codebase, and the
# permission each use needs:
#
# ┌────────────┬────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Permission │   Level    │                    Used for                      │
# ├────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Contents   │ Read and   │ worker-entrypoint.sh's git remote set-url with   │
# │            │ write      │ the token — cloning, branching, committing,      │
# │            │            │ pushing                                          │
# ├────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Issues     │ Read and   │ github.js's fetchTicket/postComment/             │
# │            │ write      │ createSubIssue; gh issue create/close/comment    │
# ├────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Pull       │ Read and   │ gh pr create/view/diff/comment; watch-feedback.js│
# │ requests   │ write      │ polling PR merge/close state                     │
# ├────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Webhooks   │ Read and   │ watch-feedback.js registers/deletes repo         │
# │            │ write      │ webhooks per-PR (the trycloudflare tunnel)       │
# ├────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Metadata   │ Read-only  │ Mandatory baseline — every fine-grained PAT      │
# │            │            │ requires this, no write option exists            │
# └────────────┴────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: the dispatch daemon also needs these. They can live here for fully
# non-interactive startup, or stay in your shell profile.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=
# LINEAR_TEAM_ID=
